        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "They're adjectives: they **agree** in gender and number and usually go **before** the noun: **la segunda vuelta**, **los primeros días**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Primero → primer** and **tercero → tercer** before a **masculine singular** noun: **el primer día, el tercer lugar**. The feminine never shortens: **la primera vez, la tercera clase**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Without a noun, use the full form: **Llegué primero. Quedé tercero.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Abbreviations: **1.º, 1.ª, 1.er** (for **primer**), **2.º, 2.ª**…"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "After **décimo**, people usually just use the normal number after the noun: **el piso doce**, **el capítulo quince**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **primer** and **tercer** lose their tail only in front of a masculine noun."
        }
      ]
    },
